@*
    Switching between the light and the dark theme.

    One partial in two presentations, because the control belongs in two quite different places.
    Signed in it is an item in the user menu, between Change Password and Logout. Signed out there
    is no menu, so it is a button of its own in the header: the catalogue, signing in, signing up
    and recovering a password are all read by people with no account, and how a page looks is not
    something to hold behind one.

    Pass "item" for the menu form and "button" for the standalone one. A model is always required:
    a partial called without one inherits the model of the page it sits on, which here would be
    whatever that page happens to be.

        <partial name="_ThemeSwitch" model="@("item")" />
        <partial name="_ThemeSwitch" model="@("button")" />

    Both faces are rendered and the CSS shows whichever matches the theme in force. That is what
    lets the switch flip instantly without a reload: site.js changes one attribute on <html> and
    the label and icon follow, with nothing to swap by hand.
*@
@model string
@{
    var asMenuItem = Model == "item";

    var currentTheme = ResearchPublicationManagementSystem.Services.SiteTheme.For(Context);
    var otherTheme = ResearchPublicationManagementSystem.Services.SiteTheme.Opposite(currentTheme);

    // Back to the page it was pressed on, so the switch never moves anybody off what they were
    // reading. Only used when the form actually submits, which is the no-JavaScript path.
    var here = $"{Context.Request.Path}{Context.Request.QueryString}";

    var buttonClass = asMenuItem
        ? "dropdown-item d-flex align-items-center gap-2"
        : "btn btn-icon btn-ghost-secondary rpms-theme-button";
}

<form asp-controller="Theme" asp-action="Set" method="post" class="m-0" data-rpms-theme-form>
    <input type="hidden" name="theme" value="@otherTheme" />
    <input type="hidden" name="returnUrl" value="@here" />

    <button type="submit" class="@buttonClass"
            title="@(currentTheme == "dark" ? "Switch to the light theme" : "Switch to the dark theme")">

        @* Shown while the light theme is in force: pressing this goes dark. *@
        <span class="rpms-when-light d-flex align-items-center gap-2">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon" width="18" height="18"
                 viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" fill="none"
                 stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke="none" d="M0 0h24v24H0z" fill="none" />
                <path d="M12 3c.132 0 .263 0 .393 0a7.5 7.5 0 0 0 7.92 12.446a9 9 0 1 1 -8.313 -12.454z" />
            </svg>
            @if (asMenuItem)
            {
                <span>Dark theme</span>
            }
            else
            {
                @* The icon alone in a header, where a word would crowd the brand. The title and
                   this label carry the meaning for anybody not reading the picture. *@
                <span class="visually-hidden">Switch to the dark theme</span>
            }
        </span>

        <span class="rpms-when-dark d-flex align-items-center gap-2">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon" width="18" height="18"
                 viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" fill="none"
                 stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke="none" d="M0 0h24v24H0z" fill="none" />
                <path d="M12 12m-4 0a4 4 0 1 0 8 0a4 4 0 1 0 -8 0" />
                <path d="M3 12h1m8 -9v1m8 8h1m-9 8v1m-6.4 -15.4l.7 .7m12.1 -.7l-.7 .7m0 11.4l.7 .7m-12.1 -.7l-.7 .7" />
            </svg>
            @if (asMenuItem)
            {
                <span>Light theme</span>
            }
            else
            {
                <span class="visually-hidden">Switch to the light theme</span>
            }
        </span>
    </button>
</form>
